<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iuput II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iuput II was a king in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> in the late 8th century BCE, usually located at Leontopolis and assigned to the Twenty-third Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. He was one of the local rulers who joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tefnakht">Tefnakht</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> and then submitted to the Kushite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye</a> during his campaign of about 728 BCE, as recorded on Piye's Victory Stela.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iuput-ii.jpg" alt="Iuput II" width="320" height="535" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: IuputII-Relief_BrooklynMuseum.png: Keith Schengili-Roberts derivative work: JMCC1 (talk) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IuputII-Relief_BrooklynMuseum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
